---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="klyna.dev is essentially cookieless. The admin panel uses one CSRF/session cookie."
  heading="Cookie Policy"
>
  <p>
    <strong>klyna.dev is essentially cookieless.</strong> We do not use tracking cookies, advertising
    cookies, or analytics cookies. The only cookie we set is a single session cookie on the admin
    panel, used by the studio operator to stay logged in.
  </p>

  <h2>The full list</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Where</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Lifetime</th>
        <th>Type</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>klyna_session</code></td>
        <td><code>klyna.dev/admin</code> only</td>
        <td>Holds an opaque session id so the admin operator stays logged in and CSRF is enforced.</td>
        <td>Session, or 15 min idle, whichever is shorter</td>
        <td>Strictly necessary (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    That is the whole list. We do not use Google Analytics, Plausible, Fathom, or any other
    analytics tool on klyna.dev. We do not embed Facebook pixels, LinkedIn tags, or ad-network
    snippets. Nothing third-party fires on page load.
  </p>

  <h2>What about the plugins and apps?</h2>
  <p>
    Klyna plugins and apps run inside your WordPress site or Shopify store. Any cookies they
    interact with belong to that environment (WordPress login, Shopify cart) and are governed by
    your site's own cookie policy. We do not set any tracking cookies on your visitors' browsers.
  </p>

  <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>
    Since we do not track in the first place, the Do Not Track header is moot. We respect it
    anyway.
  </p>

  <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@klyna.dev">privacy@klyna.dev</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
